# R23 the funny people of the eve: Gaunt, Quill, Pip and Barnaby. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ gaunt
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Sergeant Gaunt, commanding the rear. Do not fret over the front line. I am well behind it, and I have the whole view in hand.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_menu
* [if item:wv_last_letters and not flag.letter_gaunt] Hand over the letter from his mother -> vigil/letters:to_gaunt
* Ask how the rear guard is placed -> gaunt_position
* Ask for a soldier's advice -> gaunt_advice
* Wish him luck -> END

~ gaunt_position
sgt_gaunt [neutral]: Behind the carts, behind the line, behind the houses, and if the wind turns, behind the hill. A sound tactician keeps solid ground between himself and the trouble. Preferably an entire parish.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_advice
sgt_gaunt [sly]: When the front gives way, fall back to a stout position. When the stout position cracks, fall back to a stouter one. Thirty years I have practiced the disciplined withdrawal, and nothing has caught me yet.
-> gaunt_menu

~ quill
ambrose_quill [smile]: They mean to burn the roof over our heads, and I have finished the elegy. The metre holds. I call it "Lament for the Round", though by the third stanza it has turned into a marching song.
-> quill_menu

~ quill_menu
* Ask him to read the verses -> quill_elegy
* [if flag.wv_vol_asked and not flag.vol_quill] Ask him to sign the militia roll -> quill_sign
* [if item:wv_last_letters and not flag.letter_quill] Hand him the publisher's letter -> vigil/letters:to_quill
* Leave him to his verses -> END

~ quill_elegy
Narrator: He climbs onto a dry barrel, clears his throat of the peat smoke, and reads aloud. The first stanza weeps for the timber, the second for the bones, and by the fourth the bucket line is stamping in time to the rhyme.
if not flag.quill_blessed
Narrator: Your blood answers the beat against your better judgment. For a dirge, it makes a remarkably fine charge.
bless party 2h
set quill_blessed
endif
-> quill_menu

~ quill_sign
ambrose_quill [sad]: I shall put my name down, provided the ledger notes my "Lament" as the official company hymn. It is only proper. Nobody else has written us one.
* [Performance DC 13] Promise his title a grand flourish in the margin -> quill_signed | quill_sulk
* Promise to write the hymn into the roll yourself -> quill_signed

~ quill_signed
Narrator: His signature claims the entire margin in wet black ink, underscored twice with a blot at the tail.
set vol_quill
set vol_signed += 1
-> quill_menu

~ quill_sulk
ambrose_quill [sad]: That had all the grace of a clerk's sneeze. Not a flourish in it.
-> quill_sign

~ pip
pip_oakum [smile]: I have one hundred and twelve buttons in my tin, and I am trading for nerve. Who here is the bravest? I can spare three good ones for the top sort.
-> pip_menu

~ pip_menu
* Ask where the buttons came from -> pip_buttons
* [if not flag.pip_traded] Trade him for his best button -> pip_trade
* Wish him luck -> END

~ pip_buttons
pip_oakum [neutral]: The horn one came off a captain's greatcoat. The pewter one came off a dead man's cuff. The brass one came off the church vestry door, and it stays warm in your palm. That one is the pick.
-> pip_menu

~ pip_trade
pip_oakum [smile]: You take the warm brass one. All you owe me is to walk back down that hill and tell me how it went.
Narrator: He drops a heavy brass button into your palm. Sure enough, the metal holds a hearthside warmth.
give wv_pip_button
inspiration party
set pip_traded
-> pip_menu

~ barnaby
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: Pennywhistle's Wicker Man Repellent! Two gold the phial, five the crate, gratis to the frail and the doomed. Warranted against dry rot, bailiffs, and as of dusk, giant burning effigies. Freshly inked on the label.
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_menu
* [if gold >= 5 and not flag.barnaby_sold] Buy a bottle for five gold -> barnaby_buy
* [if flag.wv_vol_asked and not flag.vol_barnaby] Ask him to sign the militia roll -> barnaby_sign
* Ask what goes into the bottle -> barnaby_what
* Leave him to his pitch -> END

~ barnaby_what
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: Sour cider, pickled verjuice, and two drams of a tincture the magistrate asked me never to name in court. Frankly, the pasteboard label does the heavy lifting.
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_buy
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: A patron of science. Agitate the sediment before uncorking. Do not take internally, and fling generously toward whatever is trying to eat you.
gold -5
give wv_barnaby_repellent
set barnaby_sold
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_sign
barnaby_pennywhistle [neutral]: Enlist? I am a purveyor of ordnance, not a footman. Though if Tamsin's roll enters me as quartermaster on retainer, I might be persuaded.
* [Persuasion DC 13] Argue that a purveyor is only a volunteer on credit -> barnaby_signed | barnaby_no
* Promise to note a bulk order beside his name -> barnaby_signed

~ barnaby_signed
Narrator: He signs his name with the neat, hook-nosed hand of a man initialing a bill of sale in his own favour.
set vol_barnaby
set vol_signed += 1
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_no
barnaby_pennywhistle [sad]: Charming sophistry, friend. It would never survive an audit.
-> barnaby_sign
